{"id":"KITH-1ln3.18","title":"kith-tui: status says Connected while API calls fail","description":"Rehearsal1 check g: during a 3 s chinwag outage two of three clients still showed 'Connected' while each logged ~600 failed Message/changes (logs/kith-bob.log 13:44:59-13:45:02). Status is driven only by SseStatus, and the SSE stream (through socat) did not notice the outage until 13:45:12; failed API calls never touch the status. Failed calls are also retried immediately with no backoff (queued StateChanges drained at ~200 req/s; a failed chat-switch load retries every 50 ms tick).

Fix: any failed JMAP call (other than 401, see KITH-1ln3.17) marks the status 'Server unreachable (retrying)'; SSE-driven work is coalesced per type and held back by an exponential backoff (1 s doubling, 30 s cap) that also gates chat-switch reloads; on the next success the status returns to Connected (or Reconnecting if SSE is still down). Test: the backoff schedule bound and a 60 s simulated outage making a bounded number of requests.

Evidence: /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mark-PROJECT-chinwag/d56f3967-d390-456c-a3d8-9501efe458da/scratchpad/rehearsal1/logs/kith-bob.log, logs/kith-carol.log, shots/07-*-restart.txt.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","owner":"mark@reviewcommit.com","created_at":"2026-10-30T13:58:22.697267604Z","created_by":"agent","updated_at":"2026-10-30T13:58:22.697267604Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"KITH-1ln3.18","depends_on_id":"KITH-1ln3","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-10-30T13:58:22.740834183Z","created_by":"agent","metadata":"{}"}]}
